{
 "help": "usage: wgsextract example-genome download [-h] [--tag TAG] [--all] [--method {auto,https,aspera}]\n                                          [--force] [--dry-run] [--help-all]\n                                          [EXAMPLE_ID ...]\n\npositional arguments:\n  EXAMPLE_ID            Example IDs to download. Defaults to a small starter set.\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --tag TAG             Download every example with this tag. May be repeated (e.g. --tag pacbio).\n  --all                 Download every curated example, including large full-genome data.\n  --method {auto,https,aspera}\n                        Transfer method. Auto is an alias for HTTPS and does not probe Aspera; use\n                        --method aspera explicitly for Aspera.\n  --force               Discard existing and partially downloaded files and download again.\n                        Without it, completed files are kept and interrupted downloads resume.\n  --dry-run             Print the planned downloads without creating files.\n  --help-all            Show this help with the advanced options too, and exit.\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\n2 advanced options not shown; 'wgsextract example-genome download --help-all' lists them.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract example-genome download na12878-lowcov-bam\n  wgsextract example-genome download na12878-lowcov-bam --dry-run\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  Into <mygenomes_library>/test-1000genomes/<example id>/, with a genome\n  config file.\n\nneeds:\n  no external tools; depending on options and inputs, also: curl; depends on\n  download speed.\n",
